\section*{Abstract}
RTE-9K is a real-time conservation and stability kernel operating in Continuous
Yield Mode (CYM). It ingests multimessenger telemetry, enforces covariant
conservation laws, preserves a topological metric-innate helicity invariant,
and maintains global eigenvalue stability via coupled $M$–$D$–$K$ dynamics.
This document defines the kernel architecture, governing equations, and
real-time execution loops.

